&lt;li&gt;Growth Experience: Prior experience at a growth-stage internet/software company or across multiple industries/verticals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder &amp;amp; Project Management: Excellent stakeholder management, communication, and negotiation skills, with experience working on project improvement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Queue Management: Experience working from queues and participating in incident/on-call rotations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Workplace team’s mission is to create and support work environments that are welcoming, comfortable, and intuitive. These spaces are designed to promote collaboration, well-being, and productivity while adhering to the rigorous safety, security, and confidentiality standards required of a financial services company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Workplace Experience team comprises operations, hospitality-focused and financially responsible professionals who directly shape the daily experiences of Stripes, visitors, and candidates across 20+ global office locations. This geographically dispersed team oversees facilities management, daily operations, and programs, including a culinary team dedicated to preparing nutritious meals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a strategic leader and experienced workplace manager with a high EQ who&#39;s enthusiastic about, and has a driving need to deliver, the best possible workplace experience for Stripes. You will be a key member of our Experience team and responsible for ensuring that workplace operations, experiences, facilities, and programs run smoothly at our Bengaluru office. As a business partner, you have a deep understanding of the needs, experiences, and day-to-day realities of Stripes at your location and build strong relationships not only with site leads but also with cross-functional partners across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires a high level of expertise and operational oversight—from understanding how the building functions top to bottom to governance of contractor team performance and ensuring financial accountability. Bengaluru is a complex site with a significant employee transportation program, and you will be accountable for the reliability, service quality, and continuous improvement of these operations. You will work in close strategic partnership with our integrated facilities management partner, establishing clear expectations, maintaining strong governance, addressing performance gaps, and ensuring services meet Stripe’s operational and workplace experience standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also play a critical role in managing operational incidents and disruptions. This requires remaining calm under pressure, bringing structure to ambiguity, coordinating the appropriate internal and external partners, communicating clearly with stakeholders, and translating lessons from incidents into durable operational improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A key part of the role is anticipating the needs of the business by understanding both the site and the broader context of company growth. You will gather and synthesize feedback from multiple sources to ensure the workplace strategy is informed by real insights from the ground. While enterprise workplace strategy is developed centrally, you are expected to bring informed recommendations based on local business needs and operational insight, and to own successful implementation and adoption at your site. You will develop site-level plans, surface material risks early, and provide leaders with clear recommendations and trade-offs rather than simply escalating problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee workplace operations at your site(s), providing direction on all workplace services, including building operations, front of house, shipping &amp;amp; receiving, events support, and employee health and safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sound, independent operational decisions by balancing business impact, risk, cost, and employee experience, seeking alignment when decisions create broader organizational impact or precedent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and motivate a team of workplace services professionals, providing direction, coaching, and performance management to drive team excellence and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strong relationships with internal stakeholders, including senior leadership, department heads, and cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a strong rapport with locally assigned Stripes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own operational performance for your site by monitoring service levels and utilization, identifying trends, resolving root causes, and driving continuous improvement across workplace operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively anticipate business needs by understanding both local context and company priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop thoughtful, data-informed recommendations that help shape workplace programs and experiences while maintaining alignment with global standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold workplace partners and service providers accountable for performance, ensuring contractual obligations, service levels, and operational standards are consistently achieved while driving continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with our Finance &amp;amp; Strategy partner and IFM partner to develop and oversee the opex budget for all facilities, opex, fixed assets and events of the Bengaluru office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the local site leadership team to activate the office by creating engagement, connection, and an inclusive environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft relevant communications and documentation regarding Workplace policies and programs for Stripes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure consistent execution of global workplace programs, standards, and policies at your site,&amp;nbsp; as developed by our Food, Space Planning, and Programs teams, adapting implementation to local operational requirements while maintaining alignment with enterprise objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Workplace team&#39;s goals by taking on ad hoc tasks and projects as they arise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7 years of experience in workplace/hospitality management in a fast-paced environment with a strong customer service orientation and an understanding of operational best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong demonstrated ability in facilities management, vendor, and budget management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strength in building relationships with key internal partners to ensure efficiency and understanding on cross-functional projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a team focused on customer service, hospitality, and operations, with the ability and desire to develop and coach your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to synthesize operational data, stakeholder feedback, and business context into clear recommendations that support sound decision making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An innovative mindset with the ability to drive exceptional workplace services and operational improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Google Suite, Slack and Jira&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear willingness to take a hands-on approach and dive into the details&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to influence cross-functional partners and translate enterprise strategy into effective local execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently, digging into problems to understand the root cause and delivering scalable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to thrive in a fast-paced workplace with rapidly changing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adept at using and experimenting with provided AI tools for things like, identifying practical opportunities to automate routine work, generate operational insights from workplace data, and improve the experience for employees and visitors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An innovative mindset with the ability to drive exceptional workplace services and operational improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Product Marketing team’s mission is to generate customer insights that inform Stripe’s product strategy, and lead go-to-market for our suite of products. Product Marketing is a highly cross-functional role at Stripe, partnering closely with Product and Engineering, Sales, Partnerships, Demand Generation and Campaigns to name a few. Different from many other Product Marketing teams, our team works across the entire product lifecycle, from helping shape the product, to driving launch and commercialization, to growing product adoption post-launch.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced writer to develop data-backed theses and original content pieces about how startups and AI-native businesses launch, monetize, and grow. In this role, you’ll collaborate closely with contributors across the product marketing, product, engineering, and demand generation teams to produce compelling content that engages and informs our audience. This is a unique opportunity for a collaborative writer and content producer who excels at translating complex concepts in AI, billing infrastructure, and revenue growth into accessible insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own content covering revenue strategies and pricing models, startups, and new developments in AI, working closely with product marketing to ensure our content reflects the latest industry advances and product news&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with the demand generation team to identify opportunities for new editorial series and research agendas&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pioneer new content formats for Stripe, including short-form content and multimedia projects that grow our audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the data science team and third-party agencies to surface relevant insights for existing and potential customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure consistency and tone in messaging across Stripe channels, including blogs, guides, reports, and social-native content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a pipeline of content, ensuring clear communication and visibility across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong writer with 7+ years of experience in journalism, content marketing, or related fields, ideally with a focus on fintech or emerging technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An analytical thinker who can derive original insights from data and market signals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled at combining various requests and feedback into a unified message&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high quality bar for differentiated content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about technology and eager to understand exactly how it works&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discerning and constructive when giving edits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiastic about developing new ways to engage and inform audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven when making decisions and assessing impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented and consistent in your work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited to work in a fast-paced environment where your efforts contribute to a greater goal and align with the company’s mission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The AI Transformation Owner drives the end-to-end AI agenda for the field organization, translating emerging AI capabilities into concrete enablement roadmaps, field use cases, and org-level strategy. You will partner closely with product and engineering teams to pilot and scale AI solutions, own the operational transformation plan needed to embed AI into day-to-day field workflows, and establish the governance framework that keeps AI adoption safe, compliant, and aligned with company standards. This is a hands-on role for someone who can move from strategy to execution without heavy oversight.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role reports to the Vice President, Enablement &amp;amp; AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Enablement Roadmap:&lt;/strong&gt; Own and continuously evolve the roadmap for AI-driven enablement initiatives, prioritizing based on field impact, feasibility, and alignment with broader Enterprise AI team and strategy..&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Field Use Cases:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify, scope, and execute on high-value AI use cases for the field (e.g., deal support, prospecting, content generation, guided selling, skills, change management), working with stakeholders to define success criteria and measure impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Field Champions: &lt;/strong&gt;build relationships with champions in the field organization to activate power-usage and drive peer-led adoption; track this adoption (e.g., usage, proficiency, behavior change) with our AI Ops Specialist and Enablement Analyst.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ops Transformation Plan:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and drive the operational plan that turns AI pilots into scaled, repeatable processes, coordinating across enablement, ops, and technical teams to remove execution bottlenecks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Governance:&lt;/strong&gt; Influence and lead governance standards for AI tool adoption in the field, including data usage, risk review, tool vetting, and alignment with company-wide AI policy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mid-Senior Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Several years of experience in enablement, sales operations, or a related GTM function, with a track record of owning initiatives end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Solutions Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Direct experience evaluating, piloting, or deploying AI tools or solutions in a business context, with a solid technical understanding of how they work and where they add value. Act as the field&#39;s primary advocate for AI tools (e.g., AI-assisted prospecting, call intelligence, forecasting copilots, RFP/proposal generation).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to work closely with product and engineering teams, translating field needs into technical requirements and vice versa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Self-Sufficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Comfortable operating with significant autonomy — able to define scope, structure ambiguous problems, and drive work forward without needing detailed direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Organization &amp;amp; Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong project management instincts; able to manage multiple workstreams (roadmap, use cases, ops transformation, governance) in parallel without dropping details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovative Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; A builder&#39;s orientation toward new technology — curious about what&#39;s possible, willing to experiment, and able to separate genuine opportunity from hype.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enablement/Sales Background:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with field or sales enablement motions (onboarding, tool adoption, content, coaching) and how AI can realistically augment them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GitLab Values Alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to work in an all-remote, asynchronous environment, leaning heavily on transparency and collaboration as defined in the GitLab Handbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Enablement &amp;amp; AI function is part of the CRO organization. Enablement is instrumental in helping GitLab grow at a more accelerated pace and achieve our ambitious revenue targets. The enablement organization comprises enablement leads serving the CRO business functions, a centralized content group, AI tech resources, and an operations team.&lt;/p&gt;
