&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cloudflare is looking for a Strategy Manager to join the Developer GTM Strategy &amp;amp; Incubation team, focused on Technical Programs. This person will help Solutions Architects, Forward Deployed Engineers, Professional Services, and Developer GTM leadership identify the right customer opportunities, organize technical GTM work, and turn high-value customer engagement into repeatable programs and operating rhythms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Developer GTM Strategy &amp;amp; Incubation function exists to evolve the way the Developer GTM team works, designing systems, processes, and GTM motions that accelerate consumption at Cloudflare. This role is focused on the technical side of that motion: where we should spend time, how we coordinate technical resources, how we run customer-facing programs, and how we measure whether technical work is driving the right business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The right person is a high-agency operator with strong technical fluency. They do not need to be a Solutions Architect, but they should be comfortable working with technical products, customer architectures, implementation workflows, developer platforms, and customer-facing technical teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and scale technical programs: &lt;/strong&gt;Design proactive programs for Solutions Architects, Forward Deployed Engineers, and related technical GTM teams. Turn ad hoc motions into repeatable playbooks, operating rhythms, and ownership models where it makes sense.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coordinate strategic customer engagement:&lt;/strong&gt; Project manage high-priority customer initiatives that require technical GTM support. Clarify goals, stakeholders, timelines, resourcing, risks, success criteria, and follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Plan and scale technical onsite visits:&lt;/strong&gt; Build the planning model for strategic customer onsites, including intake, agenda design, staffing, prep, execution, post-onsite follow-up, and measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve prioritization and visibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Own a clear view of active technical engagements, upcoming opportunities, blockers, outcomes, and resourcing needs. Partner with Revenue Engineering, Data, Sales Strategy, and technical leaders on account propensity, engagement tracking, dashboards, and operating reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support Professional Services packaging and commercialization: &lt;/strong&gt;Partner with Professional Services, Finance, Product, Sales Strategy, and GTM leaders on pricing, packaging, business cases, rollout plans, and feedback loops for technical services offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incubate and launch new technical programs:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead high-priority projects across Developer GTM, support team planning and process improvements, turn technical activity into clear business narratives, and incubate new motions until they are measurable and ready for durable ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Examples of projects this person may own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a proactive SA/FDE engagement program for a priority customer segment or product motion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner on an account propensity model that helps determine SA/FDE prioritization, resourcing, and account coverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up a technical engagement tracker for active customer work, resourcing, blockers, and outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design the planning and follow-up model for technical onsite visits with strategic customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Professional Services to package a repeatable services motion and build the business case for rollout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solutions Architects and FDEs have a clearer operating model for proactive programs and strategic customer engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership has a reliable view of technical revenue pipeline, engagement health, account propensity, and investment ROI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic customer initiatives and technical onsite visits move faster because goals, staffing, owners, success criteria, and follow-up are clear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional Services offerings are easier to understand, price, package, and align to Cloudflare&#39;s broader consumption-led strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New technical GTM motions move from ambiguous ideas to measurable programs with durable owners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Desirable Skills, Knowledge, and Experience&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;At Cloudflare, we know that great candidates come from diverse backgrounds with non-linear paths. You don’t need to tick every single box to be right for this role. If you are excited about building a better Internet and ready to make an impact, please apply.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in GTM strategy, business operations, revenue operations, technical program management, solutions strategy, consulting, or a similar cross-functional execution role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with technical customer-facing teams such as Solutions Architects, Sales Engineers, Forward Deployed Engineers, Professional Services, Customer Engineering, Developer Relations, or Product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical fluency, including the ability to understand customer architecture discussions, implementation tradeoffs, developer platform concepts, and the operating needs of technical GTM teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong program management ability, including managing complex work streams, driving accountability without direct authority, and keeping teams aligned under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong sense of ownership; someone who takes initiative, works independently, and manages time effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent cross-functional communication skills and the ability to influence and align stakeholders at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly customer-centric, with natural curiosity about technical products and a strategic mindset for solving complex problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working under pressure and adjusting priorities to meet deadlines in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, including comfort using spreadsheets, CRM data, and business dashboards to prioritize work and inform decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience with Salesforce CRM, Tableau, BigQuery, or BoostUp is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in SaaS or Product-Led Growth (PLG) is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compensation may be adjusted depending on work location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For Bay Area based hires: Estimated annual salary of $161,000 - $221,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For NYC based hires: Estimated annual salary of $153,000 - $210,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Equity&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is eligible to participate in Cloudflare’s equity plan.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Benefits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cloudflare offers a complete package of benefits and programs to support you and your family.&amp;nbsp; Our benefits programs can help you pay health care expenses, support caregiving, build capital for the future and make life a little easier and fun!&amp;nbsp; The below is a description of our benefits for employees in the United States, and benefits may vary for employees based outside the U.S.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Health &amp;amp; Welfare Benefits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical/Rx Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dental Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vision Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible Spending Accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commuter Spending Accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fertility &amp;amp; Family Forming Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On-demand mental health support and Employee Assistance Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global Travel Medical Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Financial Benefits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Short and Long Term Disability Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life &amp;amp; Accident Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) Retirement Savings Plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Stock Participation Plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Time Off&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible paid time off covering vacation and sick leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leave programs, including parental, pregnancy health, medical, and bereavement leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;What Makes Cloudflare Special?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re not just a highly ambitious, large-scale technology company. We’re a highly ambitious, large-scale technology company with a soul. Fundamental to our mission to help build a better Internet is protecting the free and open Internet.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://blog.cloudflare.com/protecting-free-expression-online/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Galileo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;: Since 2014, we&#39;ve equipped more than 2,400 journalism and civil society organizations in 111 countries with powerful tools to defend themselves against attacks that would otherwise censor their work, technology already used by Cloudflare’s enterprise customers--at no cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cloudflare.com/athenian/&quot;&gt;Athenian Project&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;: In 2017, we created the Athenian Project to ensure that state and local governments have the highest level of protection and reliability for free, so that their constituents have access to election information and voter registration. Since the project, we&#39;ve provided services to more than 425 local government election websites in 33 states.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://1.1.1.1/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1.1.1.1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;: We released&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://1.1.1.1/&quot;&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;1.1.1.1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; to help fix the foundation of the Internet by building a faster, more secure and privacy-centric public DNS resolver. This is available publicly for everyone to use - it is the first consumer-focused service Cloudflare has ever released. Here’s the deal - we don’t store client IP addresses never, ever. We will continue to abide by our&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/1.1.1.1/privacy/public-dns-resolver&quot;&gt; privacy commitment&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; and ensure that no user data is sold to advertisers or used to target consumers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Sound like something you’d like to be a part of? We’d love to hear from you!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Please note that applicants who progress to the offer stage of the interview process may be asked to attend an in-person interview within one of the Cloudflare Offices or Cloudflare Hubs.&amp;nbsp; More details about this will be available at that stage of the interview process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This position may require access to information protected under U.S. export control laws, including the U.S. Export Administration Regulations. Please note that any offer of employment may be conditioned on your authorization to receive software or technology controlled under these U.S. export laws without sponsorship for an export license.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Cloudflare is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. &amp;nbsp;We are committed to providing equal employment opportunity for all people and place great value in both diversity and inclusiveness. &amp;nbsp;All qualified applicants will be considered for employment without regard to their, or any other person&#39;s, perceived or actual&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;race, color, religion, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, physical or mental disability, medical condition, family care status, or any other basis protected by law. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We are an AA/Veterans/Disabled Employer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Cloudflare provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. &amp;nbsp;Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job. Examples of reasonable accommodations include, but are not limited to, changing the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. &amp;nbsp;If you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job, please contact us via e-mail at &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;hr@cloudflare.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; or via mail at 101 Townsend St. San Francisco, CA 94107.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Us&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we are on a mission to help build a better Internet. Today the company runs one of the world’s largest networks that powers millions of websites and other Internet properties for customers ranging from individual bloggers to SMBs to Fortune 500 companies. Cloudflare protects and accelerates any Internet application online without adding hardware, installing software, or changing a line of code. Internet properties powered by Cloudflare all have web traffic routed through its intelligent global network, which gets smarter with every request. As a result, they see significant improvement in performance and a decrease in spam and other attacks. Cloudflare was named to Entrepreneur Magazine’s Top Company Cultures list and ranked among the World’s Most Innovative Companies by Fast Company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we’re not looking for people who wait for a polished roadmap; we’re looking for the builders who see the cracks in the Internet that everyone else has simply learned to live with. We value candidates who have the instinct to spot a &quot;normalized&quot; problem and the AI-native curiosity to create a solution using the latest tools. Our culture is built on iteration, leveraging AI to ship faster today to make it better tomorrow, while ensuring that every improvement, no matter how small, is shared across the team to lift everyone up. If you’re the type of person who values curiosity over bureaucracy, and that AI is a partner in solving tough problems to keep the Internet moving forward, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(230, 126, 35);&quot;&gt;Available Locations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Switzerland&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(230, 126, 35);&quot;&gt;About the Role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;doc-paragraph&quot;&gt;We are seeking a commercially sharp and technically curious Digital Natives Account Executive to join our Swiss Sales Team, focused on the German-speaking market. In this high-energy, hunter role, your primary mission is new logo acquisition — finding, engaging, and closing net-new digital-native companies across the region who are not yet working with Cloudflare. Your target universe includes fintechs, SaaS platforms, AI-native startups, developer-led scale-ups, and cloud-first businesses: companies that move fast, make infrastructure decisions at the engineering level, and expect their vendors to keep up. The ideal candidate understands how digital-native companies actually buy — bottom-up product adoption, engineering influence, founder-driven decisions, and rapid procurement — and engages as a credible peer in conversations with CTOs, VPs of Engineering, and technical founders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;doc-paragraph&quot;&gt;As a Digital Natives Account Executive, you will build pipeline through outbound prospecting, community engagement, and ecosystem presence, convert developer-led adoption into commercial new logo wins, and position Cloudflare as the infrastructure partner of choice for the next generation of technology companies. Critically, you will use AI tools as an active and integral part of how you sell — both because your buyers, who are often building AI products themselves, will notice and respect it, and because winning new logos at pace in this segment requires it. In line with Cloudflare&#39;s AI-native culture, you are expected to leverage AI tools daily as a genuine force multiplier across your prospecting, pipeline, and preparation — not as an occasional aid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(230, 126, 35);&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;New Logo Acquisition:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive the identification, pursuit, and closure of net-new digital-native accounts as the primary focus of this role. Build pipeline through outbound prospecting, community engagement, VC and accelerator networks, partner channels, and product-led adoption signals. Consistently bring new customers onto the Cloudflare platform and exceed new logo targets each quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Outbound &amp;amp; Ecosystem-Led Pipeline Generation: &lt;/strong&gt;Take full ownership of pipeline creation — through direct outreach, active participation in the startup and tech ecosystem, and engagement with founder and developer communities across DACH. Identify buying signals early and move quickly to engage the right stakeholders at the right moment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Developer &amp;amp; Technical Buyer Engagement:&lt;/strong&gt; Build credible, trusted relationships with technically sophisticated buyers — CTOs, VPs of Engineering, platform leads, and technical founders. Engage with genuine fluency on infrastructure, APIs, developer experience, cloud architecture, and security — translating Cloudflare&#39;s capabilities into outcomes that matter to people who build things.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product-Led Growth Conversion: &lt;/strong&gt;Identify accounts where individual or team-level usage of Cloudflare&#39;s platform signals a commercial opportunity. Convert that adoption into formalised new logo wins by engaging the right stakeholders with the right narrative at the right time, before a competitor does.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Platform Positioning: &lt;/strong&gt;Position Cloudflare&#39;s AI infrastructure capabilities — AI Gateway, Workers AI, Vectorize, and Zero Trust for AI workloads — to prospects building AI-powered products and services. Understand the real challenges your customers face around securing AI APIs, managing inference at scale, and controlling AI infrastructure costs, and articulate how Cloudflare addresses them in a way that resonates with technical buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Powered Sales Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Leverage AI tools as a deliberate and consistent part of how you prospect and sell — applying them to target account research, personalised outreach at scale, technical meeting preparation, pipeline management, and follow-up drafting. Your buyers are often building AI products; your workflow should reflect the same standard. Demonstrated AI fluency is a genuine expectation of this role, and you will be asked to speak specifically to how you use AI to improve your performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full-Cycle Sales Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Run efficient, full-cycle sales processes across a diverse prospect portfolio with varying deal sizes and cycle lengths. Qualify rigorously, engage the right stakeholders, apply appropriate urgency, and close new logo deals with confidence — whether the cycle takes two weeks or six months.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compelling Value Creation: Articulate clear, outcome-linked value propositions for Cloudflare&#39;s platform, tailored to the specific context and priorities of each prospect. Lead with the &quot;why,&quot; communicating the full picture to both technical and commercial stakeholders at every stage of the sales cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Post-Close Positioning: &lt;/strong&gt;Ensure newly closed customers are set up for success on the Cloudflare platform and positioned for long-term growth. Identify early expansion signals and hand off cleanly — then focus on the next new logo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pipeline Management &amp;amp; Forecasting: &lt;/strong&gt;Maintain a healthy, accurate new logo pipeline and deliver reliable, insight-driven forecast calls to sales leadership. Use AI-powered pipeline intelligence tools to keep your view of the business current, honest, and actionable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Insight &amp;amp; Team Contribution:&lt;/strong&gt; Share field intelligence from the digital-native ecosystem openly with the wider team. Contribute to Cloudflare&#39;s understanding of how this segment builds, buys, and scales — and help the organisation stay relevant and competitive in a fast-moving market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(230, 126, 35);&quot;&gt;Desirable Skills, Knowledge, and Experience&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of experience in B2B technology sales, with a consistent track record of meeting or exceeding new logo and quota targets, ideally selling to digital-native, developer-led, startup, or scale-up companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven hunter mentality in a digital-native or startup context — you know how to find the right companies, get in front of the right people, and close before the window closes. You build your own pipeline and do not wait for inbound.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of how digital-native companies buy — product-led growth, bottom-up adoption, engineering influence, founder decision-making, and fast-moving procurement cycles. You engage as a peer, not a vendor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort engaging with technical buyers — CTOs, VPs of Engineering, platform leads, and founders — on infrastructure, APIs, developer tooling, cloud architecture, and security. You do not need to write code, but you think like someone who does.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated use of AI tools in a sales context — outreach drafting, account research, meeting preparation, pipeline management. This is a genuine requirement; be prepared to discuss specifically which tools you use and how they improve the quality and pace of your new business activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI infrastructure concepts — inference APIs, vector databases, LLM cost management, AI security — and the ability to engage credibly with customers who are building AI-powered products and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the startup or VC ecosystem is a strong advantage — you understand how these companies are funded, how they make decisions, and what they genuinely care about.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Cloudflare&#39;s developer platform (Workers, R2, Pages, AI Gateway) or competitive equivalents (Fastly, AWS CloudFront, Akamai, Zscaler) is highly advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Salesforce or equivalent CRM; familiarity with AI-powered sales tools (intelligent CRM enrichment, AI writing assistants, automated account research platforms).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly self-motivated, entrepreneurial, and technically curious — you are genuinely interested in what your prospects are building and how Cloudflare fits into it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coaching and knowledge-sharing instincts, with a passion for contributing to the team&#39;s collective intelligence and go-to-market effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel within the DACH region and to industry events as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Language Skills: German &amp;amp; English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
